# +-------------------------------------------------------------------------+
# | spine: a backend data gatherer for Cacti                                |
# +-------------------------------------------------------------------------+
# | This poller would not have been possible without:                       |
# |   - Larry Adams (current development and enhancements)                  |
# |   - Rivo Nurges (rrd support, mysql poller cache, misc functions)       |
# |   - RTG (core poller code, pthreads, snmp, autoconf examples)           |
# |   - Brady Alleman/Doug Warner (threading ideas, implementation details) |
# +-------------------------------------------------------------------------+
# | Settings                                                                |
# +-------------------------------------------------------------------------+
# | DB_Host         'localhost' or socket file for UNIX/Linux               |
# |                 IP Address for Windows                                  |
# | DB_Database     Database name, typically 'cacti'                        |
# | DB_Port         The database port to use                                |
# | DB_User         The user to access the database, typically 'cactiuser'  |
# | DB_Pass         The password for the Cacti user                         |
# | SNMP_Clientaddr Bind SNMP to a specific address for sites that use      |
# |                 higher security levels                                  |
# | Cacti_Log       Optional path to the Cacti log file                     |
# +-------------------------------------------------------------------------+
# | Settings for Remote Polling                                             |
# +-------------------------------------------------------------------------+
# | RDB_Host        The remote database hostname.                           |
# | RDB_Database    The remote database name, typically 'cacti'             |
# | RDB_Port        The remote database port to use                         |
# | RDB_User        The remote database user, typically 'cactiuser'         |
# | RDB_Pass        The remote database password.                           |
# +-------------------------------------------------------------------------+

DB_Host       localhost
DB_Database   cacti
DB_User       cactiuser
DB_Pass       cactiuser
DB_Port       3306
#DB_UseSSL    0
#DB_SSL_Key
#DB_SSL_Cert
#DB_SSL_CA
# Explicit policy overrides legacy connector defaults; unset keeps compatibility.
# Unsupported explicit modes fail; see docs/operations/database-tls.md.
# verify-full requires a trusted DB_SSL_CA and a matching server identity.
#DB_SSL_Mode required
#DB_SSL_MinVersion TLSv1.2
#DB_SSL_Cipher ECDHE-RSA-AES128-GCM-SHA256
#DB_SSL_Ciphersuites TLS_AES_128_GCM_SHA256

# Optional structured logging. Default text preserves existing log consumers.
# JSON records use UTC timestamps and retain valid UTF-8. Invalid UTF-8 emits
# a structured error record instead of the original message.
#Log_Format text
# Optional per-command limits. Zero/unset preserves legacy script behavior.
# Enabling any limit requires complete bounded output and successful child exit.
# Resource caps (CPU, memory, file size, descriptors) require Linux /bin/sh.
#Script_DeadlineSeconds 0
#Script_OutputBytes 0
#Script_CPUSeconds 0
#Script_MemoryKiB 0
#Script_FileKiB 0
#Script_OpenFiles 0
#SNMP_Clientaddr
#Cacti_Log     /var/www/html/cacti/log/cacti.log

#RDB_Host      localhost
#RDB_Database  cacti
#RDB_User      cactiuser
#RDB_Pass      cactiuser
#RDB_Port      3306
#RDB_UseSSL    0
#RDB_SSL_Key
#RDB_SSL_Cert
#RDB_SSL_CA
#RDB_SSL_Mode verify-full
#RDB_SSL_MinVersion TLSv1.2
#RDB_SSL_Cipher ECDHE-RSA-AES128-GCM-SHA256
#RDB_SSL_Ciphersuites TLS_AES_128_GCM_SHA256

